- [ ] Implement `:indeterminate` matching
  - checkbox with `indeterminate` property true
  - radio buttons with no selection in group
  - progress elements with no value
- [ ] Add tests for :checked/:indeterminate

### 27.4 Validity State (12 tests blocked)
Prerequisites: 27.1 (Form Element Infrastructure), HTMLInputElement.validity
- [ ] Implement `:valid` matching
  - Form elements that satisfy validation constraints
- [ ] Implement `:invalid` matching
  - Form elements that do NOT satisfy validation constraints
- [ ] Implement `:required` / `:optional` matching
  - Based on `required` attribute
- [ ] Implement `:in-range` / `:out-of-range` matching
  - For number/date inputs with min/max
- [ ] Add tests for validation pseudo-classes

### 27.5 Read/Write State (4 tests blocked)
Prerequisites: 27.1 (Form Element Infrastructure)
- [ ] Implement `:read-only` matching
  - readonly attribute OR not an editable element
- [ ] Implement `:read-write` matching
  - Editable inputs/textareas without readonly
  - contenteditable elements
- [ ] Add tests for :read-only/:read-write

### 27.6 Placeholder/Default State (4 tests blocked)
Prerequisites: 27.1 (Form Element Infrastructure)
- [ ] Implement `:placeholder-shown` matching
  - Input/textarea showing placeholder text
- [ ] Implement `:default` matching
  - Default button in form
  - Default option in select
  - Checked checkbox/radio with checked attribute
- [ ] Add tests for :placeholder-shown/:default

### 27.7 Focus State (8 tests blocked)
Prerequisites: Phase 20 (Event System)
- [ ] Implement `:focus` matching
  - Element is the current focus target
- [ ] Implement `:focus-within` matching
  - Element or descendant has focus
- [ ] Implement `:focus-visible` matching
  - Focus should be visibly indicated (keyboard navigation)
- [ ] Add tests for focus pseudo-classes

## Phase 28: User Action Pseudo-Class Selectors
Spec Reference: https://www.w3.org/TR/selectors-4/#useraction-pseudos
Prerequisites: Phase 20 (Event System)

### 28.1 Hover/Active State (14 tests blocked)
Prerequisites: Phase 20.3 (Mouse/Pointer Events)
- [ ] Add `Element.IsHovered` property (set by event handlers)
- [ ] Add `Element.IsActive` property (mousedown/touchstart active)
- [ ] Implement `:hover` matching in `PseudoClassSelector.Matches()`
- [ ] Implement `:active` matching
- [ ] Bubble state: parent of hovered element is also :hover
- [ ] Add tests for :hover/:active

### 28.2 Target Pseudo-Class (4 tests blocked)
Prerequisites: URL fragment handling, Document.location
- [ ] Implement `:target` matching
  - Element whose ID matches URL fragment
- [ ] Update on hashchange events
- [ ] Add tests for :target

### 28.3 Visited/Link State (4 tests blocked)
Prerequisites: Link history tracking (privacy considerations)
- [ ] Implement `:link` matching
  - Unvisited hyperlinks (a, area with href)
- [ ] Implement `:visited` matching
  - Visited hyperlinks
  - Note: Must limit queryable styles for privacy
- [ ] Implement `:any-link` matching
  - Any hyperlink (visited or not)
- [ ] Add tests for link pseudo-classes

## Phase 29: Selector Edge Cases & Escaping
Spec Reference: https://www.w3.org/TR/css-syntax-3/#escaping
Prerequisites: CSS Tokenizer escape sequence handling

### 29.1 Escaped Character Parsing (10 tests blocked)
- [ ] Verify tokenizer handles `\:` escape in identifiers
- [ ] Verify tokenizer handles `\.` escape in class names
- [ ] Verify tokenizer handles `\#` escape in identifiers
- [ ] Verify tokenizer handles `\ ` (escaped space) in identifiers
- [ ] Verify tokenizer handles `\\` (escaped backslash)
- [ ] Add tests: `Parse_EscapedColon_InId`, `Parse_EscapedDot_InClassName`

### 29.2 Unicode Escapes (4 tests blocked)
Prerequisites: 29.1 (Escaped Character Parsing)
- [ ] Verify tokenizer handles `\XXXXXX` hex escapes (1-6 hex digits)
- [ ] Space after hex escape terminates the escape
- [ ] Verify `\41 ` → "A" (hex 41)
- [ ] Add tests: `Parse_UnicodeEscape`

### 29.3 Unicode Identifiers (4 tests blocked)
- [ ] Verify non-ASCII characters work in identifiers
- [ ] Test CJK characters in class names: `.日本語`
- [ ] Test emoji in class names: `.🎉`
- [ ] Add tests for unicode selectors

### 29.4 Legacy Single-Colon Pseudo-Elements (4 tests blocked)
For backwards compatibility, `:before`, `:after`, `:first-line`, `:first-letter` should parse as pseudo-elements.
- [ ] Add legacy pseudo-element name check in `Consume_Pseudo_Class_Selector`
- [ ] Convert `:before` → `::before` etc. during parsing
- [ ] Add tests: `Before_SingleColonLegacy`, `After_SingleColonLegacy`

## Phase 30: Advanced DOM Selector Contexts
Spec Reference: https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#interface-documentfragment
Prerequisites: DocumentFragment implementation

### 30.1 DocumentFragment Selector Matching (3 tests blocked)
- [ ] Verify selector matching works inside DocumentFragment
- [ ] `:root` should NOT match elements in fragment (no document root)
- [ ] Descendant selectors should work within fragment subtree
- [ ] Add tests for DocumentFragment matching

### 30.2 Shadow DOM Selectors (6 tests blocked)
Prerequisites: Phase 21 (Shadow DOM)
- [ ] Implement `:host` pseudo-class
  - Matches shadow host from inside shadow tree
- [ ] Implement `:host()` functional pseudo-class
  - Matches shadow host if it matches argument
- [ ] Implement `:host-context()` pseudo-class
  - Matches if ancestor matches argument
- [ ] Implement `::slotted()` pseudo-element
  - Matches slotted content
- [ ] Verify selectors don't pierce shadow boundary
- [ ] Add tests for shadow DOM selectors

### 30.3 Namespace Selectors (4 tests blocked)
Prerequisites: XML namespace support
- [ ] Parse `namespace|element` syntax
- [ ] Parse `*|element` (any namespace)
- [ ] Parse `|element` (no namespace)
- [ ] Handle @namespace at-rule for prefix declaration
